Apply migrations from the repository root with:

    backend/.venv/bin/flask --app backend.app db upgrade

The existing revision history is already managed by Flask-Migrate; do not run
`flask db init` or stamp an existing database without checking its schema.
The default database is `instance/database.db` in the repository root. Set
`COWRITER_DATABASE_URI` to use another database.

Create a migration after changing models with:

    backend/.venv/bin/flask --app backend.app db migrate -m "describe the change"

Review the generated revision before applying it with `db upgrade`.
